-- ============================================================================
-- DR3 EXPERT DEEP SEED: Drilling Hydraulics, advanced tier.
--
-- Six modules, 26 lessons, 132 questions (15 per module bank plus a 42
-- question final exam). The structure row is GENERATED from the tier's
-- manifest.json.
--
-- What this tier owns: pressure with the pumps off, and the window all four
-- pressures share. Surge and swab are the same annular flow with the sign
-- reversed, symmetric about the static mud weight to the last digit. A CLOSED
-- string displaces its whole outside area and an OPEN one only its steel,
-- which is 0.2686329600000001 of it for this drill pipe, and the pressures
-- nevertheless differ by only about 1.17 because the Burkhardt clinging term
-- at 0.45 is present in both and does not scale with the displaced volume. The
-- pressure rises as roughly the 0.6 power of the trip speed, so slowing down
-- helps and helps less than proportionally. Four pressures have to fit between
-- the pore and fracture limits, of which the SWAB is the only one below the
-- mud weight and the one most easily forgotten. The speed limit is a bisection
-- and whichever limit sits closer to the mud weight binds.
--
-- WHAT IT NAMES AND DOES NOT CERTIFY. Transients and the acceleration term,
-- which on a 3000 m column at 0.1 m/s2 is about 432000 Pa against a steady
-- surge of about 0.98 MPa. Temperature and compressibility, of similar size
-- and opposite sign on a water-based mud and not on an oil-based one. Gel
-- strength, which is what a break-circulation pressure depends on and which
-- the yield stress is not. Eccentricity and rotation, which are conservative
-- for the pressure and optimistic for the cleaning. And cuttings beds, which
-- the Professional tier established. Expert m05 l05 states all five and the
-- go-live migration asserts that none is graded.
--
-- Numeric sweep 200 literals / 0 unresolved over the lessons; tier-leakage 0
-- downward leaks and 0 same-tier answer prints over 78 lessons and 21 banks;
-- hydraulicsLab.test.js 27 tests green; bank QA 0 duplicate or near-duplicate
-- prompts within a tier, key shares 0.212 to 0.273, 0 em dashes, 0 positional
-- references.
--
-- Answer keys live only here and in academy_quiz_questions.
-- ============================================================================

